# secrets and local data
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Interview records, and the questions written for one applicant — those reveal what
# that applicant wrote about themselves. Both belong in the operator's private
# repository (ADR-0004), never in this public one. The suffixed forms are the ones a
# person makes by hand to keep a set aside — `results.ja-sample/` and the like — which
# hold records of exactly the same shape and were slipping past the two names above.
results/
candidates/
results.*/
candidates.*/

# The server's own output. It names who applied and carries whatever an upstream API
# said back; a public repository is no place for either.
*.log

# python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/

# editors · os
.DS_Store
